        },
        {
          title: 'Embedding pages as images',
          body: 'I tested image-based and multimodal alternatives because page images preserve visual layout. Processing each page independently still separated cross-page notes from their citations. In the RAGFlow path I evaluated, a vision model converted the image to text, which was then embedded. Reconstructing the relationships explicitly in that text gave more control over which pieces retrieval could return together.'
        },
        {
